## Third-party licensing note

This license covers obs-phonecast's own code only (everything under `src/`,
`test/`, `scripts/`, and the project's own configuration and documentation
files).

obs-phonecast is an orchestration layer: it launches, monitors, and configures
**scrcpy**, but never touches a single pixel of video itself. All screen
capture, encoding, and mirroring is scrcpy's work.

- **scrcpy** is developed by Genymobile and Romain Vimont, licensed under
  **Apache License 2.0**. Copyright (C) 2018 Genymobile, Copyright (C)
  2018-2026 Romain Vimont.
- Any scrcpy (and adb) binaries fetched or bundled by this project's
  release workflow under `vendor/` remain under that same Apache 2.0
  license, accompanied by their own original `LICENSE` file. They are not
  relicensed as MIT by their presence in this repository.

If you build on this project, keep this distinction intact: MIT applies to
what obs-phonecast itself wrote, Apache 2.0 applies to scrcpy wherever it's
bundled or referenced.